{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"immortal-stony-kodiakbear","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation\n\nDuring the df72 store repair on 2026-10-28, the local `tickets` branch had local-only commits while also trailing `origin/tickets` (related history, each side with unique commits). `rebar store fsck` reported:\n\n```\nDIVERGED: local 'tickets' branch has diverged from origin/tickets — no shared history / cannot fast-forward. The local store was built independently of the remote (e.g. init could not fetch the existing branch), so it hides remote tickets and its writes will never push. Recover: run `rebar fsck-recover`, or re-clone and re-init\n```\n\n## Defects\n\n`_tracker_sync_status` in `src/rebar/_commands/fsck_tracker_health.py` uses one message for two different states:\n\n1. No common ancestor (`git merge-base` fails). The text fits this case.\n2. A common ancestor exists, but neither side contains the other. The text is false here: the histories are shared, the store was not \"built independently\", and re-cloning would discard the local-only commits, which may hold ticket events not yet on the remote.\n\nSeparately, the recovery advice names `rebar fsck-recover`, which is not a command. `rebar fsck-recover` fails with `invalid choice`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The related-but-diverged case reports its own message: local and remote share history, the counts of local-only and remote-only commits, and a non-destructive recovery path that preserves local-only commits.\n- [ ] The no-common-ancestor case keeps a message that fits it.\n- [ ] Neither message names a command that does not exist. A test checks that every rebar command named in the advice is a real subcommand.\n- [ ] Tests cover both cases.","id":"4f16-c86f-7a57-4470","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"fsck DIVERGED message claims no shared history for a related divergence and names a nonexistent recovery command"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793236100299035001,"uuid":"85ca20f9-ee2c-4c0d-895a-0e1e7206d476"}